# Level 1, climbing. A short run right along the middle row leaves the
# Prince under the near edge of the floor above -- row 0 is open at columns
# 0..2 and floor from column 3 on, so the tile above him is empty and the
# one above and in front of him is floor: a ledge to take hold of. Up is
# then held, and held again after it has run its course, so that what the
# original does with a grabbable ledge in front of it is pinned both for a
# fresh press and for a key that is simply kept down.
level 1
cycles 400
settle 40
phase - 3
phase r 4
phase - 4
phase u 10
phase - 4
phase u 8
phase - 4
